course: dictionary
lesson: 13786
title: Intro: the informal opening
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Intro is an informal word, a short form of introduction. People use it in everyday talk. «The intro of the song is my favourite part» means the opening part, the start, before the main song begins.
explain: Intro can also mean when you introduce one person to another. «Let me do the intro: this is my cousin Leo.» The words around it, like this is my cousin, tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Use context to decide which meaning is right. Then swap in another word, such as beginning or introduction, and check the sentence still makes sense. In school writing, use the full word introduction instead of intro.
fact: Intro is an informal noun, short for introduction.
fact: «Intro» means the start of a song, book, talk or video.
fact: «Intro» can also mean the moment when you introduce one person to another.
fact: In school writing, use «introduction» instead of «intro».
exercise: «The intro of the song is my favourite part.» What is an intro here? | The last note of the song | A dance move | *The start of the song | The name of the singer
exercise: Ruby says, «Let me do the intro: this is my cousin Leo.» What does intro mean here? | A type of cough | The end of a party | A long walk home | *The moment she introduces two people
exercise: Which word should you use in a school essay instead of intro? | hiccup | intermission | interval | *introduction
test: «Skip the intro, I already know the story.» What does skipping the intro mean? | Reading the story twice | *Missing the opening part and going straight on | Writing a new story | Telling the story to a friend
test: Which is the informal word for the opening part of a video? | outro | sequel | trailer | *intro
exam: What is the informal word for the ending of a video? | *outro | intermission | introvert | intro
